colorado governor jared polis just  announced that the state of colorado is  now going to begin accepting bitcoin for  tax payments starting in the summer of  2022. now jared polis is a very  interesting character when it comes to  bitcoin he was the first politician in  the united states to actually accept  bitcoin as part of his campaign  donations going all the way back to  2014. and so obviously jared polis as  the governor of colorado he's pro  bitcoin he understands what this  decentralized digital currency means for  the world now if we go ahead and we take  a look at the exact quote that he used  it's very telling he said the state  would not hold any of the assets in  crypto those would be instantly  converted back into dollars when the  transaction occurred the government  would not be interested in participating  in the speculative aspects positive or  negative we would simply use it as a  means of exchange for purposes of  payment now this is interesting because  obviously he understands bitcoin he's  accepted bitcoin as a campaign donation  but he also understands that he's  operating in a conservative environment  of politics and if he's seen to be  speculating on the price of these assets  that won't be good and likely he'll  receive pushback both from his own  political party and also the other side  of the aisle and so being able to accept  bitcoin as an exchange of payment for  those taxes but convert it into us  dollars gives him the ability to walk  the middle of the road use bitcoin as a  means of exchange but also not speculate  on price if we look at colorado they're  not exactly a small state when it comes  to actual revenues from taxes there's 58  billion dollars in combined state and  local general revenues that came from  taxes in 2019 which comes out to about  10 000  per individual within the state and so  ultimately this is exactly what i expect  to see across every single state we saw  previously the state of ohio josh mandel  who's a 